1
00:00:01,650 --> 00:00:04,240
A daily life that's taken
for granted by some...

2
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:06,480
is a world I've never known.

3
00:00:10,030 --> 00:00:11,890
Everything is a first for me.

4
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:14,160
Everything is unfamiliar.

5
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:23,520
Someday...

6
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:26,530
will I ever be able to fit into this world?

7
00:00:52,190 --> 00:00:54,010
Why is this neighborhood so empty?

8
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:27,680
Um, excuse me. Do you live around here?

9
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:29,710
It's my first time here, so...

10
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:32,320
I heard there's a big church
nearby. Do you know where it is?

11
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,470
It's just a little further that way.

12
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:40,500
Um...

13
00:01:40,930 --> 00:01:42,320
Your eyes are a little...

14
00:01:42,450 --> 00:01:43,450
different.

15
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:47,340
Are you okay?

16
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:50,640
Not interested.

17
00:01:51,750 --> 00:01:52,430
What?

18
00:01:52,431 --> 00:01:54,700
I said I'm not interested in your religion.

19
00:01:56,030 --> 00:01:57,830
Go preach somewhere else.

20
00:01:59,370 --> 00:02:00,850
I'm not feeling my best today.

21
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,440
Just cut me a break.

22
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:06,000
"My Secret Vampire"

23
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:10,500
(Episode 1)

24
00:03:14,130 --> 00:03:15,330
Ugh.

25
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:16,740
The weather is awful.

26
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,800
(A wash-off mask for
vampire-like pale skin.)

27
00:03:40,270 --> 00:03:42,649
This blood bag smells weird. Is it expired?

28
00:03:42,650 --> 00:03:44,280
We still have to make it last.

29
00:03:44,930 --> 00:03:47,010
I hear the good stuff is
hard to come by these days.

30
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:49,029
The alternative food source
will be out soon anyway.

31
00:03:49,030 --> 00:03:50,236
Just hang in there a bit longer.

32
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:52,240
Or do you want some of this?

33
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:54,260
Oh.

34
00:03:55,750 --> 00:03:56,950
Hey, but...

35
00:03:57,350 --> 00:03:58,420
that alternative food...

36
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:00,696
it should taste better
than the blood bags, right?

37
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:02,630
I hear it tastes a lot like human blood.

38
00:04:03,470 --> 00:04:04,670
Save it for later.

39
00:04:06,420 --> 00:04:10,920
I worked out today. Wanna feel?

40
00:04:11,470 --> 00:04:12,990
Hey! Get off me!

41
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:17,880
Why act like that when
we're friends here...

42
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:21,206
What? Do you just stay
home and shop online all day?

43
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:23,100
- I can do what I want.
- What's this now?

44
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,810
It's mine. Don't touch it.

45
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:35,540
Where have you been?

46
00:04:41,510 --> 00:04:42,510
What's with him?

47
00:04:42,530 --> 00:04:43,530
I don't know.

48
00:04:43,550 --> 00:04:44,550
Let's just go up.

49
00:04:44,570 --> 00:04:46,530
- Did something happen...?
- Just go up.

50
00:04:46,930 --> 00:04:47,930
I said go up.

51
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:51,110
- But I'm a little worried...
- Just go on up.

52
00:05:08,750 --> 00:05:09,750
Mr. Han Dongha.

53
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:11,420
Welcome to your new home.

54
00:05:12,110 --> 00:05:14,190
The passcode is 1917 then hashtag.

55
00:05:14,670 --> 00:05:15,670
If you have any problems,

56
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:17,950
please ask the house manager, Juwon.

57
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:21,620
Oh, right.

58
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:26,010
My younger brothers are good
kids, just a bit socially awkward.

59
00:05:26,370 --> 00:05:28,040
Please get along for the next month.

60
00:05:49,950 --> 00:05:51,050
Is anyone home?

61
00:05:53,530 --> 00:05:56,120
Why is it so dark... Is no one here?

62
00:06:22,790 --> 00:06:23,990
Hey, Sis.

63
00:06:26,210 --> 00:06:27,210
What is it?

64
00:06:27,550 --> 00:06:28,750
Who did you say was coming?

65
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:33,100
Hey! Who are you?

66
00:06:33,170 --> 00:06:34,170
I'm sorry!

67
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:39,410
I'm not feeling my best today.

68
00:06:39,930 --> 00:06:41,410
Just do me a favor and go.

69
00:06:47,230 --> 00:06:51,580
Excuse me... are you the umbrella thief?

70
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:54,980
Are you... from a cult?

71
00:07:03,870 --> 00:07:04,430
What's wrong?

72
00:07:04,430 --> 00:07:05,430
What's going on?

73
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:19,460
My name is Han Dongha.

74
00:07:20,630 --> 00:07:21,889
I have a job interview,

75
00:07:21,890 --> 00:07:23,170
so I came a little early.

76
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:29,080
I told the landlord, but I guess
she hasn't told the other tenants yet.

77
00:07:29,610 --> 00:07:31,290
Enough with the landlord and tenant talk.

78
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:35,170
You think I'd fall for a trick like that?

79
00:07:35,250 --> 00:07:37,900
Hey, I'm the one who got ripped off.

80
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,770
So stubborn.

81
00:07:39,910 --> 00:07:41,830
You don't happen to have
a cross on you, do you?

82
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:45,060
It's contraband in this house,
so get it out of here now.

83
00:07:47,530 --> 00:07:49,260
Wow, now you're framing me.

84
00:07:49,330 --> 00:07:52,650
- I told you I'm not in a cult. I'm the new tenant.
- We're not looking for tenants.

85
00:07:54,060 --> 00:07:55,700
Get out of here before I stop being nice.

86
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:58,980
Oh, Sis.

87
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:00,020
What are you doing here?

88
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:03,690
Mr. Han Dongha?

89
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:04,900
Yes!

90
00:08:06,620 --> 00:08:07,620
It's nice to meet you.

91
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,600
Alright.

92
00:08:21,050 --> 00:08:22,270
For the next month,

93
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:24,890
- let's all get along, okay?
- Yes!

94
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:27,160
- Answer me.
- Yes!

95
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:28,440
Sis.

96
00:08:28,990 --> 00:08:30,490
You didn't even discuss this with us.

97
00:08:32,310 --> 00:08:33,850
You, come with me for a second.

98
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:43,330
If you hate blood bags that much, you
should at least take your medicine on time.

99
00:08:43,410 --> 00:08:46,330
Why are you so disobedient,
always fainting in the sun?

100
00:08:47,020 --> 00:08:48,220
Are you trying to defy me?

101
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:50,540
I didn't pass out, I
just got a little dizzy.

102
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:52,290
Don't talk back. From now on,

103
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:53,596
you are not to draw the curtains.

104
00:08:53,620 --> 00:08:55,420
You must take your
medicine before going out.

105
00:08:55,850 --> 00:08:56,690
If you dare break the rules,

106
00:08:56,691 --> 00:08:57,850
I'll kick you out myself.

107
00:08:58,070 --> 00:08:58,990
Why?

108
00:08:59,010 --> 00:09:02,010
Didn't you say you'd go to college
once the alternative food was developed?

109
00:09:03,070 --> 00:09:04,270
There's only one month left.

110
00:09:04,670 --> 00:09:06,480
You should start getting used to things.

111
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:09,400
That alternative food... will it
really be okay for me to eat it?

112
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:12,080
Are you doubting my skills now?

113
00:09:14,250 --> 00:09:15,230
No, that's not it.

114
00:09:15,231 --> 00:09:17,690
I'm not a pure-blood like them.

115
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:19,439
There might be side effects or something.

116
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:23,499
I made it so that even a
half-human like you can enjoy it.

117
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:24,840
So don't worry.

118
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:28,410
Okay, I get it.

119
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:30,420
But what's the deal with that human?

120
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:32,509
We were doing fine on our
own, so why all of a sudden...

121
00:09:32,510 --> 00:09:33,510
Back in the day,

122
00:09:34,270 --> 00:09:37,879
back in Gyeongseong, we built our
own little village and lived just fine.

123
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:39,080
But what about now?

124
00:09:39,650 --> 00:09:45,430
There are security cameras everywhere. Even
grannies in the mountains are live streaming.

125
00:09:45,730 --> 00:09:48,760
Do you think it's possible to live
without any contact with humans?!

126
00:09:48,850 --> 00:09:49,850
Is it?

127
00:09:50,790 --> 00:09:52,250
Stop building walls around yourselves.

128
00:09:52,270 --> 00:09:53,900
Hurry up and face reality.

129
00:09:55,140 --> 00:09:57,130
He's just one human. What's the big deal?

130
00:09:57,820 --> 00:09:59,690
You're making a mountain out of a molehill!

131
00:09:59,910 --> 00:10:00,830
Oghwi.

132
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:01,850
Sehee.

133
00:10:02,170 --> 00:10:03,390
I changed my name.

134
00:10:04,070 --> 00:10:05,290
Fine, whatever.

135
00:10:05,710 --> 00:10:07,316
Don't come crying to me
when I suck his blood one day.

136
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:12,130
Oh, please. Look who's talking.
You can't even stand blood bags.

137
00:10:16,290 --> 00:10:18,359
You can't have his anyway.

138
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:21,030
So give up and try to get along.

139
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:26,430
But don't get too attached.

140
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:33,280
So you're not a cultist.

141
00:10:33,310 --> 00:10:37,520
Or do you have other religious
beliefs, or dream of being a clergyman?

142
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:38,320
Do you like garlic?

143
00:10:38,321 --> 00:10:40,060
Can you read a room?

144
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:43,480
I'm not religious, and as for garlic...
But why do you ask...?

145
00:10:44,710 --> 00:10:47,560
No reason, just asking.

146
00:10:48,230 --> 00:10:49,230
Let's get along.

147
00:10:49,660 --> 00:10:51,670
- Let's get along.
- You too.

148
00:11:01,050 --> 00:11:02,050
One month.

149
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:03,280
Right?

150
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:04,560
Yes.

151
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:07,040
There's just one thing you have to follow.

152
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:11,650
Never interfere in each
other's private lives.

153
00:11:12,230 --> 00:11:13,990
Break that rule, and
you're out immediately.

154
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:17,790
But what exactly falls
under 'private lives'?

155
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:21,490
Try not to get involved with
the people who live here.

156
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:24,720
It'd be even better if you could
pretend you don't know us.

157
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:26,370
Is that a rule?

158
00:11:26,470 --> 00:11:27,540
It is now.

159
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:28,800
I just made it.

160
00:11:31,930 --> 00:11:33,220
And one last thing.

161
00:11:33,550 --> 00:11:34,800
There's one more person.

162
00:11:35,130 --> 00:11:36,410
Don't even look at him.

163
00:11:38,110 --> 00:11:39,310
You guys, come with me.

164
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:46,670
Hey, what's his deal?

165
00:11:47,070 --> 00:11:48,070
Isn't it obvious?

166
00:11:48,110 --> 00:11:49,670
He's low on hemoglobin.

167
00:11:49,790 --> 00:11:51,090
What's with that guy...

168
00:12:45,610 --> 00:12:47,520
What are you doing out here so late?

169
00:12:50,490 --> 00:12:53,070
I guess I can't sleep well in a new place.

170
00:12:58,670 --> 00:13:01,400
Wow, even the air in Seoul feels different.

171
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:02,380
I'm from the countryside.

172
00:13:02,381 --> 00:13:04,010
This is my first time in a big city.

173
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:07,530
But we get to see a lot
of stars where I'm from.

174
00:13:14,290 --> 00:13:17,560
You're a freshman at
Hanguk University too, right?

175
00:13:18,610 --> 00:13:19,810
The landlord told me.

176
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:26,840
Oh, but about that umbrella earlier...

177
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:36,860
The money for the umbrella...

178
00:13:37,330 --> 00:13:39,340
No, no, that's not what I meant.

179
00:13:42,010 --> 00:13:43,850
Let's not have anything
to do with each other.

180
00:13:52,050 --> 00:13:54,030
I was just going to ask if you were okay...

181
00:14:36,100 --> 00:14:39,100
"My Secret Vampire"

